  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive). Pattern: Xを{促|うなが}す / XにYを{促|うなが}す.\n\nUSAGE:\nSense 1 takes a person as the indirect object and an action as the direct object: {彼|かれ}に{決断|けつだん}を{促|うなが}す (to urge him to decide). Sense 2 takes an abstract process as the direct object: {成長|せいちょう}を{促|うなが}す (to promote growth).\n{促|うなが}す is more formal and measured than {急|せ}かす (to rush someone). It implies a respectful push rather than impatient pressure.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {注意|ちゅうい}を{促|うなが}す: to call attention to, to urge caution\n- {返事|へんじ}を{促|うなが}す: to press for a reply\n- {発言|はつげん}を{促|うなが}す: to prompt someone to speak\n- {避難|ひなん}を{促|うなが}す: to urge evacuation\n- {成長|せいちょう}を{促|うなが}す: to promote growth",
